+
+At draw time, deterministic health showed 40 sampled cases, 39 outcomes filed, zero findings and one overdue-to-be-reported case (#255); no ordinary watchdog incident. After filing, all four sampled cases have outcomes: #255 `not_assigned`, child and #6 initially `finding`, and the government decision `verified` (scoped to artifact presence). Both findings were subsequently corrected to `not_assigned` under Act 17 after a fresh assignment/origin review. The same office confirmed both corrections; that is procedural, not independent verification. Current health reports zero active findings and retains two `corrected_finding` signals. `sh tests/run-all.sh` passed after reporting, including randomized-accountability, board-trail, host-CI-policy, and continuity smoke checks (exit 0; expected fixture diagnostics included simulated invalid credentials, empty-repository and unavailable-origin conditions). Full reassessment and command outputs are in `records/AUDIT-2026-10-23-reassessment.md`.
